  "summary": "India competes across nine sports on Day 4 of the Commonwealth Games 2026, with medal hopes in athletics, weightlifting and gymnastics. Follow live scores, event schedules and rolling updates on India\u2019s performances.",
  "content": "India are competing across nine sports on Day 4 of the Commonwealth Games 2026, with medal prospects highlighted in athletics, weightlifting and gymnastics. The delegation includes a mix of experienced campaigners and emerging talents aiming to add to the medal tally as the tournament progresses.\n\nAthletics is expected to be a focal point today, with Indian athletes taking part in multiple track and field events. Several competitors are targeting finals and podium finishes, and fans will be watching qualification rounds and timed events closely for signs of medal contention.\n\nWeightlifting remains another strong area for India, where the team will contest multiple weight categories across the session. Performances in the snatch and clean and jerk will determine medal outcomes, and coaches are closely monitoring attempts and strategy as lifters chase personal bests and national records.\n\nIn gymnastics, Indian entrants will look to deliver clean routines in both individual and apparatus competitions. Execution and consistency will be key as gymnasts aim to translate difficulty into scoring and challenge for places on the podium.\n\nFor followers at home, live scores and rolling updates will be provided throughout the day. Coverage includes real-time results, medal standings, and summaries of key performances. Stay tuned for updates as results come in and athletes conclude their events on Day 4.",
